  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tuberculosis - Bolivia (Plurinational State) (01-Jan-2017-31-Dec-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bolivia (Plurinational State), Tuberculosis, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Bolivia)This program has the following goals: Reduce the incidence of all forms of TB by 17% by 2020.  Reduce the mortality rate from TB/HIV by 15%. The objectives of this program are: Offer integrated TB/HIV care service, ensuring the continuity of the cooperation and joint management mechanism between the TB/HIV programs; to reduce the TB burden in people with HIV, and to reduce the HIV burden in people with TB.  Offer services for the care, case detection, diagnosis and treatment of TB, to reduce the burden of all forms of TB.  Strengthen the offering of MDR-TB care services, with early diagnosis, case detection, guaranteeing treatment and monitoring, to reduce the burden of MDR-TB</narrative>
  </description>
